1.0.0+mc26.2
- Armor value and armor toughness of every equipped piece now scale with that piece's remaining
  durability using multiplier = 1 - (1 - r)^2, where r = remaining / max durability.
- Knockback resistance is unaffected.
- Tooltips now show the loss: below the vanilla blue `+N Armor` / `+N Armor Toughness` lines, red
  `Wear: -N Armor` / `Wear: -N Armor Toughness` lines report what the piece has already lost to
  durability (zh_cn: `耐久损耗：-N 护甲值` / `耐久损耗：-N 盔甲韧性`). A pristine piece adds nothing;
  hiding the attribute lines hides these lines too; the numbers are derived from the same scaling the
  runtime applies, so they cannot disagree with the live value.
- Additive attribute modifiers (ADD_VALUE, ADD_MULTIPLIED_BASE) are scaled; ADD_MULTIPLIED_TOTAL
  modifiers are left unchanged, so a piece's final contribution is exactly `original value ×
  multiplier` for the vanilla `(base + Σ add) · (1 + Σ total)` formula.
- Unbreakable items get no exemption: they use the same remaining/max durability ratio as any other
  stack (ordinary unbreakable gear carries no damage, so its multiplier is 1).
- Implemented as a single hook on ItemStack#forEachModifier(EquipmentSlot, BiConsumer), the vanilla
  funnel that applies equipment attribute modifiers, so nothing permanent is written to items or
  entities and client and server stay in sync without custom packets.
- Works with vanilla armor and with armor from other mods that uses the standard attribute-modifier
  component.
